# Project Structure

1. Component Creation
Create all components as React components in the src\business-apps folder.
Each component should extend its props from the `BusinessAppContextProps` interface.
Whenever an access token is required, use it from the `BusinessAppContextProps` interface.
Whenever an user, an user info or an employee ID is required, use it from the `BusinessAppContextProps` interface.

All folders in src\business-apps folder are products that we have, e.g. crm, irm etc.
All folders in src\business-apps\<product> are either named `components`, `modules`, `hooks`, `libs`, `utils`, `overview-screens`, `detail-screens`, `flow-screens` or contain the name of the component.
All files in src\business-apps\<product>\<screenName> are files related to that screen where one `.tsx` with the name of screen is located and an `index.ts` file with a named export of the component and a default export of the component.
Example of correctly create components:
- src\business-apps\irm\detail-screens\LeadDetail\LeadDetail.tsx
- src\business-apps\irm\overview-screens\LeadOverview\LeadOverview.tsx
- src\business-apps\crm\overview-screens\OpportunityOverview\OpportunityOverview.tsx

2. Component Dependencies
Use react for UI components
Use ant-design for React UI components
Use @dnd-kit for drag and drop
Use zustand for state management in React
Use react-dom for working with the DOM
Use react-router-dom for routing
Use typescript for type safety
Use prettier for code styling
Use eslint for linting

Do not install other packages for UI themes, icons, etc. unless absolutely necessary or I request them.
The list of required dependencies must be small and simple and must reuse existing packages.

3. Component Development
Always prefix all CSS classes with the `gba:` prefix.

Whenever an input field is used to provide search by an user, use the existing `DebouncedInput` component to provide debounced search.

When tab components are used, provide a unique hash for each tab to allow direct navigation to the tab via URLs.

Everytime data querying with GraphQL is needed, use the newwork-graphql-mcp plugin.

4. Component Publishing
Use the script npm run publish:screen -- **/<ScreenFolder> to publish or deploy a screen, a component and or an app.

